From 69e0260101bdc344c547a7d2f628e25346053280 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: terminills <tdeters@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 13 Jul 2026 21:21:46 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 163/638] content: use native AROS crash reporting in shell
 [chromium] [aros]

Statement: AROS content_shell faults are reported by debug.resource and expanded by OPAL; Crashpad's POSIX mmap, paths, and UUID substrate is neither available nor the native reporting path.

Decision: Omit Crashpad app/browser dependencies and initialization on AROS while retaining crash-key support. Keep Chromium web-test-only clients excluded consistently in both GN and ShellMainDelegate.

Evidence: The windowed build failed in Crashpad close_stdio, uuid, and file_io_posix; regeneration then exposed web-test Mojo headers despite support_web_tests=false.

Validation: gn gen out/aros-windowed --root-target=//content/shell:content_shell; content_shell graph contains no Crashpad client/util; shell_main_delegate.o compiles.

Chain:; ACD-chromium-aros-native-crash-reporting
